@page
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
    ViewData["Description"] = "What aibysitter and its GitHub App read, keep and log.";
}

<h1>Privacy</h1>

<h2>Lint page</h2>
<ul>
    <li>With JavaScript on, the file is linted in your browser. The text is not sent.</li>
    <li>With JavaScript off, the server lints it. The text is never stored or logged. Request logs record IP address, path and status for 14 days.</li>
    <li>Share links put the text, format and rule choices in the URL after #. Browsers do not send that part to the server. Anyone with the link can read the text.</li>
    <li>Lint by URL and badges: the server fetches the file from raw.githubusercontent.com, so GitHub sees the request come from this site. For public files it finds, it stores the repository name, file name, score, grade, ruleset version and time, kept up to 400 days, and shows them as score history. Private repositories cannot be read, so nothing is stored for them. The repository name is not logged.</li>
    <li>One cookie: the lint form's anti-forgery token. No analytics, no tracking scripts.</li>
</ul>

<h2>API</h2>
<ul>
    <li>The text is not stored or logged. Request logs record IP address, path and status for 14 days.</li>
</ul>

<h2>GitHub App</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Reads, at the pull request's head commit: the changed files and their diff, rules files, and <code>.github/aibysitter.json</code>. For R006 it also reads the repository file list and the manifests a rules file refers to (<code>package.json</code>, Makefiles, <code>.gitignore</code>, MSBuild files).</li>
    <li>Holds a queue file for the duration of a review: repository, pull request number, commit, check run ID and delivery ID. It is deleted when the review completes.</li>
    <li>Stores nothing else. Logs record repository, pull request number, commit, delivery ID and finding count for 14 days. No file contents are logged.</li>
    <li>Results are posted to GitHub as a check run on the pull request.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Permissions</h3>
<table class="stack">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>Permission</th>
